meta {
  name: List a user's games
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/users/{{username}}/games
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  The whole library, unpaginated by design: the browser filters, groups and sorts
  it client-side in `pipeline.ts`, so the API hands over the full array and the
  page narrows it.

  Play state (`currentlyPlaying`, `lastPlayed`, `playingSince`, `openSessionId`,
  `sessionCount`) is derived from `play_sessions` in the service layer, never
  stored, so it cannot disagree with the sessions themselves.

  Row `id`s are exposed on a public read on purpose. They grant nothing: every
  mutation re-checks ownership against the caller's token and 404s otherwise.

  - 200 a list of games (empty for a user with none)
  - 404 no such username
}
